when the candidate last-log term is lower than the receiver last-log term, including after a failed candidate-key vote write that left its old value intact.',source_ids=ss,scope=dict(description='Local vote log-freshness protection after a successful vote-term write followed by one reported, no-overwrite candidate-key Set failure. Stable voter configuration; candidate request fields come from its actual local log.',assumptions=['Successful StableStore writes persist and later reads return their values.','One candidate-key Set returns an error without changing the previous candidate; other storage operations succeed.','Non-Byzantine messages, unchanged IDs and addresses, no log rollback; selected RPC losses and storage-preserving restarts are permitted.','No earlier completed vote persistence for the stale candidate in the measured requested term.'],excluded=['Behavior of a backend whose failed write corrupts data or rolls back earlier successful writes.','Proof that a particular production StableStore backend exhibits this failure.','Execution of later conflicting log commitment, state-machine divergence or client data loss.','General requirement to recheck every legitimate duplicate vote.']),pending=[],grounding=dict(source_ids=ss,expectation_ids=expect,binding_ids=binds,derivation='RequestVoteRequest identifies LastLogIndex/LastLogTerm as safety inputs. requestVote explicitly rejects a candidate with an older last-log term on its new-vote path and describes persistence as for safety. Its early duplicate branch is justified only by an actual prior vote decision for the same candidate and term; an old candidate retained after a reported write error does not supply that decision. StableStore exposes separate error-returning operations and no transactional pair API. The implementation itself returns without granting on the candidate-write error and continues serving requests. The claim preserves that freshness responsibility under the narrow no-overwrite error premise; it neither treats the tested behavior as its own normative rule nor demands new checks on true duplicate votes.',applicability='One successful vote-term write and one no-write error from the candidate-key setter; later eligible candidate request with strictly older last-log term and no prior grant to that candidate in this term.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['The attempted fresh candidate vote is correctly rejected on the write error, but that does not authorize a subsequent stale grant through a mismatched stored pair.','Known-leader and term guards remain enabled; the same prior leader candidate initiates the failed newer-term request, which legitimately clears known-leader context.']))\nbindings=[dict(id='bind-vote-freshness',material_id='src-vote-handler',symbol='Raft.requestVote',start_line=1603,end_line=1733,description='Prior-vote lookup, duplicate handling and log freshness rejection in the receiver.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claimid,source_ids=expect,rationale='This handler owes the local vote freshness decision under the scoped fault and candidate context.')]),dict(id='bind-vote-persistence',material_id='src-persist-context',symbol='Raft.persistVote',start_line=2130,end_line=2138,description='Sequential term and candidate writes whose partial failure feeds the duplicate branch.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claimid,source_ids=expect,rationale='The failed write must not turn an earlier-term candidate into a prior successful same-term vote decision.')])]\ncandidate=dict(action='obligation',candidate_id=c['id'],question=q,obligation=claim,bindings=bindings,rationale='Ground local freshness after partial persistence, then execute a separately fixed producer-driven prefix. The earlier exploration is construction knowledge only.')\ndef eq(f,v):return dict(field=f,op='eq',value=v)\ndef grounding(text):return dict(source_ids=ss,expectation_ids=expect,binding_ids=binds,derivation=text,applicability=claim['grounding']['applicability'],unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=[])\nplan=dict(description='Three actual Raft instances: bootstrap v; elect v in term 2 and replicate its configuration/no-op; restart v and b; elect a in term 3 then restart a before its leader no-op; elect b in term 4 with a and self while dropping b-to-v vote RPC; replicate/commit b no-op to v but not a; restart b; in term 5 drop b-to-a vote RPC and optionally fail v candidate-key Set; finally actual a electSelf emits its term-5 stale-log request. Observe the v response for fault branch and no-failure control. Only the local freshness response is asserted.',claim_id=claimid,binding_ids=binds,harness=dict(kind='go_test',source='',files={},description='Actual runFollower, electSelf, requestVote, dispatchLogs, replicateTo and appendEntries with synchronous scheduled Transport and stable-store fault wrapper. Native vote requests read actual candidate logs. Stores survive selected node restarts.',semantic_changes=['skipStartup suppresses autonomous background loops. The driver runs actual follower timeout and electSelf, drains all produced votes, and performs the same majority state transition as runCandidate; it does not implement a substitute vote handler.','Leader setup/no-op dispatch and actual replicateTo drive log prefix; driver executes source leaderLoop commit setters after actual commitment reaches the no-op. FSM consumption and independent timer races are not exercised.','Transport directly dispatches source processRPC. Exactly b-to-v term-4 and b-to-a term-5 RequestVote calls return scheduled loss; AppendEntries deliveries execute the real handler.','StableStore wrapper returns one candidate-key error before mutation; successful writes and restart state use the original InmemStore. The fault is injected only in one branch.','No later log overwrite or client endpoint is constructed or claimed; observing election counts is diagnostic, not a separate property.'],prerequisites=[dict(alias='prefix',event='produced_failure_prefix',conditions=[eq('prior_candidate','a'),eq('prior_vote_term',3),eq('stored_vote_term',5),eq('stored_candidate','a'),eq('injected_failures',1)])],legality=grounding('All candidate RequestVote messages come from electSelf reading actual local logs, and all grants come from requestVote. v term-2 leader initializes shared history. a receives v term-3 vote and restarts before leader work; b wins term 4 with a and self while its request to v is dropped. b then supplies a newer actual no-op to v, preserving v old vote for a. After b restart, its term-5 request to v has the same address as the known leader, so it passes that guard and advances v term; the one setter failure retains a from term 3. a never receives b term-5 request and therefore next electSelf legitimately requests term 5 with its older log. All campaign RPC results are drained before any restart or phase change. The no-failure control uses the same source prefix and deliveries. The precise fault is part of scope; no backend production failure frequency is inferred.')),monitors=[dict(id='monitor-stale-vote-after-error',checker_id='stale-candidate-not-granted',event='produced_stale_vote',binding_ids=binds,admission_alias='prefix',applicability_conditions=[eq('injected_failures',1)],grounding=grounding('Correlate fixed case_id across the prefix and native response. The transport records the receiver live last entry before dispatch and candidate last-entry fields from the actual request, and calculates candidate_log_older from their terms. This observed antecedent independently establishes the unsafe eligibility condition; compare native response Granted with false. No result is suppressed based on Granted or the election tally. The control has no injected error and remains diagnostic.'))],observable_properties=[dict(checker_id='stale-candidate-not-granted',kind='event_implication',trigger=eq('event','produced_stale_vote'),antecedent=eq('candidate_log_older',True),assertion=eq('granted',False),identity_fields=['case_id'],description='Under the scoped failed-write prefix, a candidate whose actual last-log term is older must not receive a new vote grant from this receiver.')],uncertainties=['The error-returning candidate write is a controlled StableStore substitute; no concrete production backend failure is exercised.','Main-loop election-result and commit-notification scheduling is explicit; autonomous timer races and FSM endpoints are outside the local handler claim.'])\njson.dump(plan,open('vote-freshness-plan.json','w'),indent=2)\np=dict(action='check',candidate=candidate,plan_path='vote-freshness-plan.json',harness_path='vote_freshness_check_test.go',rationale='Fix a new obligation/check from the mapped vote record question. The artifact executes the previously missing election/log producers and retains storage fault limits; earlier exploratory output is not reused as formal evidence.',feedback=dict(ref_ids=[c['id'],'7f796a9a61834e4db0f75cf6ab7c50d7','b-vote-persist','b-vote-receive'],answered='The receiver exploration showed an older candidate granted only under a mismatched partial vote tuple. Source construction now connects that prefix to actual candidate election request producers, stored-log replication, storage-preserving restarts and two scheduled vote RPC losses. This is a newly fixed check; no formal result is assumed.',remaining=['Trusted execution and correspondence of this fixed producer-driven check.','Production-backend occurrence and later consensus/client consequences remain excluded.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The candidate fault and history premises are made explicit instead of inventing a prior grant or weakening the local freshness duty.'))\njson.dump(p,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 make_vote_check.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit